1
00:00:07,665 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,225 --> 00:01:39,025
ADAPTED FROM <i>THE EARLY SPRING</i> ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:02:44,345 --> 00:02:48,265
THE FIRST CUP OF OSMANTHUS MILK

4
00:02:49,665 --> 00:02:52,025
This bag is too expensive.
I can't take it.

5
00:02:54,705 --> 00:02:55,825
So you won't take the bag,

6
00:02:56,665 --> 00:02:58,225
but you want to talk about feelings?

7
00:03:08,385 --> 00:03:09,505
Take the bag.

8
00:03:10,385 --> 00:03:11,225
Give me a loaf of bread.

9
00:03:13,265 --> 00:03:15,025
You bought all those loaves.

10
00:03:15,105 --> 00:03:16,225
Can't I take one?

11
00:03:18,705 --> 00:03:21,185
MORE BEAUTY IN LIFE

12
00:03:35,905 --> 00:03:37,225
I'll get going, then.

13
00:03:48,825 --> 00:03:53,145
So he just gave you a bag
and said nothing more?

14
00:03:55,705 --> 00:03:56,825
Don't overthink it.

15
00:03:57,345 --> 00:03:58,905
Men usually aren't good with words.

16
00:03:59,505 --> 00:04:02,705
Maybe he just wanted to give you a bag.

17
00:04:05,985 --> 00:04:10,065
But I saw a lot of gift boxes
in his trunk.

18
00:04:10,665 --> 00:04:14,145
Maybe he keeps them handy
to buy people's silence.

19
00:04:16,825 --> 00:04:18,825
For a payoff this expensive,

20
00:04:20,265 --> 00:04:22,785
I'll definitely keep
his little mistake a secret.

21
00:04:25,225 --> 00:04:27,505
Tao, could you have misunderstood him?

22
00:04:30,585 --> 00:04:31,585
I don't know.

23
00:04:32,505 --> 00:04:34,065
And I don't want to know.

24
00:04:36,185 --> 00:04:38,225
I don't want anything that isn't mine.

25
00:04:42,825 --> 00:04:43,785
Tao.

26
00:04:46,385 --> 00:04:49,025
You may not be sure yet,

27
00:04:49,105 --> 00:04:50,945
and you'd deny it if I said it.

28
00:04:51,665 --> 00:04:54,665
But Tao, the truth is,

29
00:04:54,745 --> 00:04:55,705
you're not someone who fools around.

30
00:04:56,505 --> 00:05:00,105
You've fallen for him, haven't you?

31
00:05:00,665 --> 00:05:02,345
Whether I like him doesn't matter.

32
00:05:02,865 --> 00:05:05,345
I just feel stupid.

33
00:05:06,225 --> 00:05:08,985
Stupid enough to have
unrealistic fantasies about him.

34
00:05:22,025 --> 00:05:23,905
The misattribution of arousal theory says

35
00:05:25,905 --> 00:05:28,505
that what we feel when we're in danger

36
00:05:31,065 --> 00:05:32,225
isn't necessarily love.

37
00:05:37,585 --> 00:05:40,905
I'll still see him at work every day.

38
00:05:40,985 --> 00:05:42,785
I feel awkward just thinking about it.

39
00:05:43,425 --> 00:05:44,865
Shang Zhitao,

40
00:05:44,945 --> 00:05:48,465
you could become
an industry leader someday.

41
00:05:48,545 --> 00:05:50,305
Why let this bother you?

42
00:05:50,385 --> 00:05:51,585
Someday,

43
00:05:51,665 --> 00:05:54,065
when you make hundreds,
even thousands of times more,

44
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:56,345
you can buy me full-price bread.

45
00:05:58,265 --> 00:05:59,705
I'll buy you the most expensive kind.

46
00:05:59,785 --> 00:06:01,385
-No discounted stuff.
-You'd better.

47
00:06:18,305 --> 00:06:20,905
HOW TO KEEP YOUR DISTANCE FROM YOUR BOSS

48
00:06:26,545 --> 00:06:27,465
KEEP BOUNDARIES CLEAR
FOLLOW THE CHAIN OF COMMAND

49
00:06:27,545 --> 00:06:28,425
USE DISCRETION WHEN REPORTING

50
00:06:28,505 --> 00:06:30,265
ADULTS DON'T NEED EVERYTHING SPELLED OUT

51
00:06:31,185 --> 00:06:33,945
PRETEND NOTHING HAPPENED
SOMETIMES YOU GROW UP OVERNIGHT

52
00:06:58,785 --> 00:07:00,345
<i>In the adult world,</i>

53
00:07:01,385 --> 00:07:04,065
<i>some things don't need to be spelled out</i>

54
00:07:05,465 --> 00:07:07,025
<i>or asked about.</i>

55
00:07:08,385 --> 00:07:09,625
<i>Shang Zhitao,</i>

56
00:07:10,505 --> 00:07:14,025
<i>you need to grow up fast.</i>

57
00:07:41,345 --> 00:07:43,545
Come on. Try my cooking.

58
00:07:43,625 --> 00:07:46,465
You need fuel to fight monsters
and level up.

59
00:07:46,545 --> 00:07:48,145
-Reporting.
-Go ahead.

60
00:07:48,225 --> 00:07:49,705
I applied for a transfer.

61
00:07:49,785 --> 00:07:50,625
Really?

62
00:07:50,705 --> 00:07:53,145
Over the weekend, I talked to HR.

63
00:07:53,225 --> 00:07:54,065
They agreed.

64
00:07:55,025 --> 00:07:56,985
So you're leaving
Luan Nian's team for good?

65
00:07:58,185 --> 00:07:59,465
I've made up my mind.

66
00:07:59,545 --> 00:08:02,665
I really like this job.
I don't want to give it up.

67
00:08:02,745 --> 00:08:05,065
But what happened between us has happened.

68
00:08:05,145 --> 00:08:06,545
I can't change it.

69
00:08:07,185 --> 00:08:11,665
I think the best thing for both of us
is to draw a clear line.

70
00:08:14,025 --> 00:08:15,385
Tao, honestly,

71
00:08:15,465 --> 00:08:16,985
what happened between you two
is only natural.

72
00:08:17,065 --> 00:08:18,905
Don't put so much pressure on yourself.

73
00:08:19,585 --> 00:08:22,425
Didn't you say that when it comes to love,

74
00:08:22,505 --> 00:08:23,945
the first one to cave in loses?

75
00:08:24,025 --> 00:08:25,025
Fair point.

76
00:08:25,105 --> 00:08:27,505
I may be a little timid
and not brave enough,

77
00:08:27,585 --> 00:08:30,065
but I know I can handle this.

78
00:08:30,145 --> 00:08:31,945
I believe you can too.

79
00:08:32,025 --> 00:08:34,664
And it'll show him
you don't let feelings control you.

80
00:08:35,385 --> 00:08:36,225
Exactly.

81
00:08:37,545 --> 00:08:38,465
Let's eat.

82
00:08:51,145 --> 00:08:52,385
Busy?

83
00:08:55,225 --> 00:08:56,105
What's up?

84
00:08:57,385 --> 00:08:58,305
Nothing major.

85
00:08:58,385 --> 00:09:00,865
I just received a transfer request.

86
00:09:00,945 --> 00:09:03,785
It's from someone on your team,
so I came to ask about her.

87
00:09:03,865 --> 00:09:04,945
Who?

88
00:09:05,785 --> 00:09:08,985
Her name is Shang Zhitao.

89
00:09:15,425 --> 00:09:18,065
Shang Zhitao applied for a transfer?

90
00:09:18,145 --> 00:09:20,065
Everyone wants to move up.

91
00:09:20,945 --> 00:09:22,465
Tracy just forwarded me
her transfer request.

92
00:09:23,785 --> 00:09:25,025
What's she like?

93
00:09:26,585 --> 00:09:28,025
I don't have time to vet her for you.

94
00:09:30,105 --> 00:09:31,745
You think that little of her?

95
00:09:32,785 --> 00:09:34,225
Not one good word?

96
00:09:36,025 --> 00:09:37,305
Fine. Got it.

97
00:09:37,945 --> 00:09:38,785
Then I don't want her.

98
00:09:40,465 --> 00:09:41,345
Wait.

99
00:09:49,985 --> 00:09:51,145
She's not exactly a natural.

100
00:09:53,225 --> 00:09:55,065
I can tell.

101
00:09:55,145 --> 00:09:57,305
But by your standards,

102
00:09:57,385 --> 00:09:59,385
there are probably only a handful
in the entire industry.

103
00:09:59,465 --> 00:10:00,745
What else?

104
00:10:03,385 --> 00:10:04,665
She's modest and never takes credit.

105
00:10:05,825 --> 00:10:06,785
She's patient.

106
00:10:07,385 --> 00:10:08,305
She never complains.

107
00:10:09,745 --> 00:10:11,025
She's persistent and hardworking.

108
00:10:12,985 --> 00:10:15,185
Sometimes she seems too willing
to put up with things,

109
00:10:15,945 --> 00:10:17,025
but she's ambitious.

110
00:10:21,225 --> 00:10:24,225
That's a pretty fair assessment.

111
00:10:25,265 --> 00:10:28,345
It's a shame she didn't stay on your team.

112
00:10:29,705 --> 00:10:30,665
Tracy,

113
00:10:30,745 --> 00:10:34,145
I'll approve Shang Zhitao's
transfer request.

114
00:10:35,305 --> 00:10:36,825
Put her in an account executive role.

115
00:10:36,905 --> 00:10:37,985
Have her start next Monday.

116
00:10:43,905 --> 00:10:44,945
Sorry to lose her?

117
00:10:45,625 --> 00:10:46,465
I don't care.

118
00:10:53,505 --> 00:10:54,545
Thanks.

119
00:11:14,025 --> 00:11:15,905
SHANG ZHITAO

120
00:11:57,625 --> 00:11:58,705
You're here early.

121
00:12:00,065 --> 00:12:01,105
Morning, Luke.

122
00:12:04,305 --> 00:12:05,625
Why did you apply for a transfer?

123
00:12:08,185 --> 00:12:09,705
I wanted a change of environment.

124
00:12:10,705 --> 00:12:12,625
Are you that eager to draw
a line between us?

125
00:12:14,625 --> 00:12:17,105
Luke, don't get the wrong idea.

126
00:12:17,185 --> 00:12:19,785
There was no other reason
for the transfer.

127
00:12:19,865 --> 00:12:22,665
It's just part of my career plan.

128
00:12:30,985 --> 00:12:32,385
Why aren't you using the bag I gave you?

129
00:12:39,265 --> 00:12:40,385
Don't worry.

130
00:12:41,545 --> 00:12:42,785
I accepted the bag.

131
00:12:43,585 --> 00:12:44,425
I'll keep your secret.

132
00:12:57,385 --> 00:12:59,785
Do you think you can only
get promoted on Alex's team?

133
00:13:01,705 --> 00:13:04,505
Whatever work I'm given,
I'll give it my all.

134
00:13:05,025 --> 00:13:07,185
Whether I get promoted is my own business.

135
00:13:08,025 --> 00:13:09,265
You can judge me by my work.

136
00:13:32,705 --> 00:13:34,145
Shang Zhitao, have you lost your mind?

137
00:13:34,225 --> 00:13:35,065
Lumi.

138
00:13:36,625 --> 00:13:39,905
Luke may have a sharp tongue,
but he's got clout.

139
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:41,705
He was just starting to warm to you.

140
00:13:41,785 --> 00:13:43,625
This is when you should
be sticking close to him.

141
00:13:43,705 --> 00:13:45,465
So why… why did you run off instead?

142
00:13:46,705 --> 00:13:49,345
I don't meet his standards anyway.

143
00:13:49,425 --> 00:13:52,305
To him, I'm hardly worth mentioning.

144
00:13:54,185 --> 00:13:55,425
Did that stubborn mule chew you out again?

145
00:13:57,065 --> 00:14:00,025
Don't let a couple of harsh words
get to you.

146
00:14:00,105 --> 00:14:00,945
Think about it.

147
00:14:01,585 --> 00:14:03,945
In Guangzhou, when that jerk tried
to force drinks on you,

148
00:14:04,025 --> 00:14:05,345
didn't Luke step in for you?

149
00:14:06,425 --> 00:14:08,265
When the shoot got hit by that downpour,

150
00:14:08,345 --> 00:14:09,865
didn't he go rescue you?

151
00:14:10,585 --> 00:14:11,905
After all that,

152
00:14:11,985 --> 00:14:13,945
even if he's a crooked old tree,

153
00:14:14,025 --> 00:14:15,785
at least he can shelter you
from the storm.

154
00:14:16,385 --> 00:14:17,505
But working with Alex?

155
00:14:17,585 --> 00:14:20,705
He's just a plastic potted plant.
All looks and no use.

156
00:14:21,465 --> 00:14:22,745
Meeting in the conference room.

157
00:14:28,065 --> 00:14:29,025
I've got a meeting.

158
00:14:33,465 --> 00:14:35,385
Well, look at that.

159
00:14:38,025 --> 00:14:38,985
Boss,

160
00:14:39,585 --> 00:14:41,625
Shang Zhitao is moving to Alex's team?

161
00:14:41,705 --> 00:14:43,665
Yes. I approved it.

162
00:14:43,745 --> 00:14:46,065
I think she's a good fit for Alex's team.

163
00:14:46,585 --> 00:14:47,945
How is she a good fit?

164
00:14:51,025 --> 00:14:52,145
Bring her back.

165
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:53,905
I'm used to working with her.

166
00:14:54,825 --> 00:14:55,945
Have you finished your work?

167
00:14:56,025 --> 00:14:57,665
Did you turn in your quarterly report?

168
00:14:57,745 --> 00:15:00,585
Get me your quarterly report in one hour.

169
00:15:00,665 --> 00:15:01,905
One hour?

170
00:15:03,185 --> 00:15:04,025
Why are you still here?

171
00:15:04,105 --> 00:15:06,225
No wonder no one wants to work for you.

172
00:15:06,785 --> 00:15:08,225
-Even I want out.
-Fifty minutes.

173
00:15:16,865 --> 00:15:20,265
OK. Before we officially begin,
let's welcome our new colleague.

174
00:15:21,145 --> 00:15:22,665
Introduce yourself.

175
00:15:22,745 --> 00:15:25,425
Hi, everyone. I'm Shang Zhitao.
My English name is Flora.

176
00:15:25,505 --> 00:15:26,665
I'll be joining as an account executive.

177
00:15:26,745 --> 00:15:29,425
Great. Annie will be
your mentor from now on.

178
00:15:29,505 --> 00:15:30,505
You'll be assigning her work.

179
00:15:30,585 --> 00:15:34,425
OK, Flora, please take the minutes
for today's meeting.

180
00:15:34,505 --> 00:15:35,585
Come to me anytime if you have questions.

181
00:15:35,665 --> 00:15:36,865
Got it.

182
00:15:37,505 --> 00:15:39,705
Remember to use the company template
for the minutes.

183
00:15:40,825 --> 00:15:42,705
Don't use the format from your old team.

184
00:15:44,505 --> 00:15:46,465
Annie, bring everyone up to speed
on this case.

185
00:15:46,545 --> 00:15:47,385
Sure.

186
00:15:47,465 --> 00:15:48,865
Could you pull up slide 5?

187
00:15:51,265 --> 00:15:53,785
The key visual for this brief
isn't working for me.

188
00:15:53,865 --> 00:15:56,705
Make it red. Give it more of a party vibe.

189
00:15:56,785 --> 00:15:58,585
The CVR and CTR need revising too.

190
00:15:58,665 --> 00:16:01,505
For the OOA,
I'm aiming for around ten million views.

191
00:16:02,105 --> 00:16:04,505
As for the PVG…

192
00:16:11,465 --> 00:16:13,305
All right. If there are no questions,
let's proceed with this plan.

193
00:16:15,665 --> 00:16:18,305
Flora, are you good with Excel?

194
00:16:19,425 --> 00:16:21,705
-Yes.
-I sent you a spreadsheet. Take a look.

195
00:16:22,665 --> 00:16:24,345
Add a column showing the profit or loss

196
00:16:24,425 --> 00:16:26,145
so the client can see
the bottom line at a glance.

197
00:16:26,225 --> 00:16:27,145
OK.

198
00:16:32,865 --> 00:16:35,545
REVENUE, EXPENSES, PROFIT

199
00:16:35,625 --> 00:16:37,025
You know formula shortcuts?

200
00:16:38,025 --> 00:16:40,025
Yes. I taught myself Excel systematically.

201
00:16:40,105 --> 00:16:43,705
I was going to ask Finance
to help me make a pivot chart.

202
00:16:43,785 --> 00:16:45,425
-Can you do that?
-Yes.

203
00:16:46,065 --> 00:16:47,465
Can you get it to me
by the end of the day?

204
00:16:48,665 --> 00:16:49,625
No problem.

205
00:17:13,625 --> 00:17:15,745
You're Flora, right? I'm Tianran.

206
00:17:17,345 --> 00:17:19,905
-What are you drinking?
-Barley tea.

207
00:17:21,424 --> 00:17:23,224
No one on our team drinks that.

208
00:17:23,305 --> 00:17:24,865
We all drink black coffee.

209
00:17:24,944 --> 00:17:26,785
It keeps us sharp
and stops us overthinking.

210
00:17:28,065 --> 00:17:30,305
I… I don't like black coffee.

211
00:17:32,825 --> 00:17:33,665
I get it.

212
00:17:34,745 --> 00:17:38,345
I heard you had a pretty rough time
on Luke's team.

213
00:17:38,425 --> 00:17:41,225
It must've been as bitter as this coffee.

214
00:17:41,305 --> 00:17:42,705
Smart move,

215
00:17:42,785 --> 00:17:44,705
jumping from the back burner
onto the fast track.

216
00:17:46,785 --> 00:17:49,345
Luke treated me well.

217
00:17:51,145 --> 00:17:52,465
He treated you well?

218
00:17:54,785 --> 00:17:58,065
I heard he went to war with the company

219
00:17:58,145 --> 00:18:00,585
because one of his subordinates
got hurt on set.

220
00:18:00,665 --> 00:18:02,065
That wasn't you, was it?

221
00:18:02,145 --> 00:18:03,665
Yes, that was me.

222
00:18:05,305 --> 00:18:06,865
Then why did you join our team?

223
00:18:09,025 --> 00:18:10,065
It's work.

224
00:18:10,145 --> 00:18:12,345
At work, don't results matter
more than the process?

225
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:16,825
You're pretty good with words.

226
00:18:18,225 --> 00:18:19,465
Want to try some?

227
00:18:19,545 --> 00:18:21,385
Barley tea is good for your stomach.

228
00:18:24,105 --> 00:18:25,105
I'll get going, then.

229
00:19:04,345 --> 00:19:06,185
MEETING MINUTES

230
00:19:17,945 --> 00:19:20,545
DU ANNI

231
00:19:21,305 --> 00:19:22,385
Annie,

232
00:19:22,465 --> 00:19:24,145
I've emailed you the meeting minutes.

233
00:19:24,225 --> 00:19:26,945
<i>Alex likes to see the minutes</i>
<i>before the end of the workday.</i>

234
00:19:27,025 --> 00:19:28,625
<i>I've finished them</i>
<i>and sent them to everyone.</i>

235
00:19:30,585 --> 00:19:31,505
I'm sorry.

236
00:19:31,585 --> 00:19:33,545
I was too slow. I'll be quicker next time.

237
00:19:34,145 --> 00:19:36,025
<i>You're new,</i>
<i>so I won't blame you this time.</i>

238
00:19:36,105 --> 00:19:37,625
<i>But you need to adapt quickly.</i>

239
00:19:38,225 --> 00:19:39,345
<i>And one more thing.</i>

240
00:19:39,425 --> 00:19:42,345
<i>Alex hates it when his people get</i>
<i>too close to colleagues on other teams.</i>

241
00:19:42,425 --> 00:19:44,905
<i>Everything you're working on</i>
<i>must remain strictly confidential.</i>

242
00:19:45,625 --> 00:19:47,865
<i>You need to remember whose team you're on.</i>

243
00:19:48,585 --> 00:19:49,825
<i>Am I making myself clear?</i>

244
00:19:52,185 --> 00:19:53,225
Yes.

245
00:19:53,865 --> 00:19:55,025
Thank you, Annie.

246
00:20:04,945 --> 00:20:06,025
<i>What's wrong?</i>

247
00:20:06,105 --> 00:20:07,585
It's only your first day
after the transfer,

248
00:20:07,665 --> 00:20:08,785
and you already look drained.

249
00:20:09,305 --> 00:20:10,145
Things didn't go well?

250
00:20:11,825 --> 00:20:13,505
Ever feel completely out of your depth?

251
00:20:14,225 --> 00:20:16,545
Is it that hard to fit in with the elite?

252
00:20:17,225 --> 00:20:19,225
What exactly is hard?
Is the workload heavy?

253
00:20:22,065 --> 00:20:23,665
My English is terrible.

254
00:20:25,345 --> 00:20:27,625
I couldn't even keep up well enough
to take the meeting minutes.

255
00:20:27,705 --> 00:20:30,465
They used so much industry jargon.
I couldn't understand.

256
00:20:30,545 --> 00:20:32,145
Industry jargon in English?

257
00:20:32,225 --> 00:20:33,905
Ask Long Zhentian
to give you a crash course.

258
00:20:33,985 --> 00:20:36,265
Long Zhentian can't help with this.

259
00:20:36,865 --> 00:20:38,225
I think you can handle it yourself.

260
00:20:39,625 --> 00:20:43,225
Every industry has its own jargon
and technical terms.

261
00:20:43,305 --> 00:20:45,585
When you're just starting out,
all the jargon can be overwhelming,

262
00:20:46,185 --> 00:20:48,505
so it's easy to think the work
is more complicated than it really is.

263
00:20:49,345 --> 00:20:50,505
Write everything down.

264
00:20:50,585 --> 00:20:52,745
Listen, read, and practice more.

265
00:20:52,825 --> 00:20:54,025
In a month,

266
00:20:54,105 --> 00:20:55,505
you'll be able to handle it with ease.

267
00:20:55,585 --> 00:20:57,425
A month is too long.

268
00:20:57,505 --> 00:20:59,705
I want to master it in a week.

269
00:21:01,025 --> 00:21:03,265
Tao, one week?

270
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:05,305
Listen. The whole world's just winging it.

271
00:21:06,025 --> 00:21:07,985
You're being too hard on yourself.

272
00:21:08,065 --> 00:21:10,185
Relax. We're all doing life
for the first time.

273
00:21:12,025 --> 00:21:14,665
Take it one step at a time.
Don't rush. It'll all work out.

274
00:21:18,185 --> 00:21:19,825
How come you have this?

275
00:21:21,825 --> 00:21:23,425
At the book stall
by Peking University's south gate,

276
00:21:23,505 --> 00:21:24,425
books were ten yuan a kilo.

277
00:21:24,505 --> 00:21:26,345
Those are all just fancy words.

278
00:21:27,025 --> 00:21:28,945
Take your time with it.
Ask me if you have any questions.

279
00:21:29,025 --> 00:21:31,025
Zhu, how are you so good at everything?

280
00:21:31,625 --> 00:21:32,825
Ms. Shang.

281
00:21:32,905 --> 00:21:34,185
Working means putting up
with a lot of grief.

282
00:21:34,265 --> 00:21:35,545
Just today,

283
00:21:35,625 --> 00:21:37,985
our accountant told me
I'd exceeded my travel allowance

284
00:21:38,065 --> 00:21:39,665
and had to pay part of it myself.

285
00:21:39,745 --> 00:21:40,585
Isn't that unfair?

286
00:21:40,665 --> 00:21:42,345
Exactly. It's totally unfair.

287
00:21:42,425 --> 00:21:43,505
My boss is the same.

288
00:21:43,585 --> 00:21:47,785
He set my monthly KPI
at 20 successful matches.

289
00:21:47,865 --> 00:21:49,665
Isn't that forcing me
to pair people up at random?

290
00:21:49,745 --> 00:21:51,025
I'm done with it.

291
00:21:51,105 --> 00:21:52,625
-Whatever happens, happens.
-Then I'm not traveling for work either.

292
00:21:52,705 --> 00:21:53,865
Whatever happens, happens.

293
00:21:54,825 --> 00:21:56,185
Work's been…

294
00:21:59,465 --> 00:22:00,945
-Go on.
-Say it.

295
00:22:01,025 --> 00:22:02,865
Work's been fine lately.

296
00:22:04,825 --> 00:22:06,265
Yuanzhu, you're not much of a team player.

297
00:22:06,345 --> 00:22:07,665
Sun Yu, take away his chopsticks.

298
00:22:07,745 --> 00:22:09,345
You're not with us.

299
00:22:13,465 --> 00:22:15,545
Fine. Then I won't
go to work tomorrow either.

300
00:22:16,265 --> 00:22:19,705
It's settled. Anyone who goes
to work tomorrow is a corporate lapdog.

301
00:22:19,785 --> 00:22:20,785
Who's a corporate lapdog?

302
00:22:20,865 --> 00:22:22,185
Who's a corporate lapdog?

303
00:22:24,385 --> 00:22:26,345
I have to work tomorrow.

304
00:22:27,545 --> 00:22:28,465
I'm the corporate lapdog.

305
00:22:29,345 --> 00:22:30,385
Get her a dog bowl!

306
00:22:31,225 --> 00:22:32,585
Bark twice, and I'll give you meat.

307
00:22:32,665 --> 00:22:34,105
-I'll get it myself.
-Go ahead.

308
00:22:35,465 --> 00:22:36,545
Pass me some salmon.

309
00:22:37,065 --> 00:22:38,105
I've got dipping sauce here.

310
00:22:38,185 --> 00:22:39,265
Anyone want some?

311
00:22:39,345 --> 00:22:40,265
-I'll take some.
-I refuse sauce offered in contempt.

312
00:22:40,345 --> 00:22:41,505
I'll take some from you.

313
00:22:41,585 --> 00:22:42,825
Do you want some or not?

314
00:22:42,905 --> 00:22:45,105
Fish balls, anyone? Do you want some?

315
00:22:50,785 --> 00:22:51,545
QIPAI JEWELRY

316
00:22:51,625 --> 00:22:52,825
We're really sorry.

317
00:22:52,905 --> 00:22:55,945
We'll revise the proposal
and get you an updated version ASAP.

318
00:22:56,025 --> 00:22:57,265
-We'll make sure you're satisfied.
-Don't bother.

319
00:22:57,985 --> 00:23:00,825
I don't think the result will be any good.

320
00:23:00,905 --> 00:23:04,745
Every revised version you've submitted
is even worse than Luke's first draft.

321
00:23:05,305 --> 00:23:06,665
Let me be direct.

322
00:23:06,745 --> 00:23:10,185
We want to go back
to Luke's original proposal.

323
00:23:17,505 --> 00:23:20,705
They want a rock-bottom price
and Luke's original proposal?

324
00:23:20,785 --> 00:23:21,905
They can't have it both ways.

325
00:23:22,585 --> 00:23:23,745
Exactly.

326
00:23:24,265 --> 00:23:25,505
And you know Luke's temper.

327
00:23:25,585 --> 00:23:27,705
Last time, when Lucy asked for some data,

328
00:23:27,785 --> 00:23:29,985
Lumi bit her head off.

329
00:23:30,065 --> 00:23:32,385
Luan Nian's proposal belongs to Lime.

330
00:23:33,465 --> 00:23:35,305
The project is with our team now.

331
00:23:35,385 --> 00:23:37,065
If he refuses to cooperate,

332
00:23:37,665 --> 00:23:38,985
he'll be costing the company the project.

333
00:23:42,225 --> 00:23:44,265
Flora used to be on Luke's team.

334
00:23:44,345 --> 00:23:45,545
She gets along with him.

335
00:23:45,625 --> 00:23:47,785
Why don't we let her try?

336
00:23:53,825 --> 00:23:54,945
She's new.

337
00:23:55,025 --> 00:23:56,025
She needs to see the bigger picture.

338
00:23:56,705 --> 00:23:58,345
When she delivers the files later,

339
00:23:59,025 --> 00:24:01,105
remind her to compliment Luke's new tie.

340
00:24:09,185 --> 00:24:12,385
<i>Most people in the company</i>
<i>are too intimidated to talk to Luke.</i>

341
00:24:12,905 --> 00:24:15,305
<i>But Li Tianran said</i>
<i>you two got along well.</i>

342
00:24:15,385 --> 00:24:16,985
Now that you're on our team,

343
00:24:18,025 --> 00:24:19,505
it's time to put that connection to use.

344
00:24:24,465 --> 00:24:25,425
We'll leave it there.

345
00:24:26,865 --> 00:24:27,705
Come in.

346
00:24:32,465 --> 00:24:33,505
Luke.

347
00:24:47,225 --> 00:24:50,585
The client from Qipai
wants to use the previous proposal.

348
00:24:51,225 --> 00:24:54,825
Could you share the source files with us?

349
00:24:59,185 --> 00:25:00,745
Did you volunteer to come,

350
00:25:01,345 --> 00:25:02,785
or did Alex send you?

351
00:25:03,865 --> 00:25:05,025
I was assigned this task.

352
00:25:07,745 --> 00:25:11,225
Did you transfer just to become
their pawn against me?

353
00:25:13,065 --> 00:25:14,345
You're reading too much into this.

354
00:25:14,425 --> 00:25:15,505
No one's out to get you.

355
00:25:17,385 --> 00:25:19,105
When Alex took you onto his team,

356
00:25:19,185 --> 00:25:20,225
didn't he make you prove your loyalty?

357
00:25:25,025 --> 00:25:27,465
Every supervisor wants loyal subordinates.

358
00:25:27,545 --> 00:25:29,465
When you were my supervisor,
I was loyal to you too.

359
00:25:31,425 --> 00:25:32,265
Fine.

360
00:25:32,345 --> 00:25:34,985
Go back and tell him
I won't give them to you.

361
00:25:35,065 --> 00:25:36,385
What do you think he'll say?

362
00:25:39,065 --> 00:25:40,825
Probably the same thing you did.

363
00:25:41,585 --> 00:25:42,985
He'll want me to quit.

364
00:25:44,865 --> 00:25:46,825
You don't have to quit.
Come back to our team.

365
00:25:47,665 --> 00:25:49,425
I'm willing to take you back,
despite everything.

366
00:25:50,025 --> 00:25:52,105
At least when it comes
to professional ethics,

367
00:25:52,185 --> 00:25:54,065
you meet my standards.

368
00:25:59,745 --> 00:26:00,825
You're a senior executive.

369
00:26:00,905 --> 00:26:02,105
You see the bigger picture.

370
00:26:02,825 --> 00:26:05,465
You can contact me anytime
if you change your mind.

371
00:26:07,465 --> 00:26:08,945
I'm not that magnanimous.

372
00:26:10,425 --> 00:26:12,585
Unlike you, I know right from wrong.

373
00:26:14,585 --> 00:26:15,825
You want the source files?

374
00:26:16,425 --> 00:26:17,545
Then wait.

375
00:26:20,785 --> 00:26:21,745
Close the door behind you.

376
00:26:31,825 --> 00:26:32,865
Stubborn.

377
00:26:34,545 --> 00:26:36,145
You want the source files
for our proposal?

378
00:26:37,105 --> 00:26:38,145
Have you no shame?

379
00:26:38,225 --> 00:26:39,985
We're just making the best use
of company resources.

380
00:26:40,785 --> 00:26:41,705
We all work for Lime.

381
00:26:41,785 --> 00:26:43,625
Besides, we wouldn't
be asking for your help

382
00:26:43,705 --> 00:26:45,705
if the client hadn't asked for them.

383
00:26:45,785 --> 00:26:46,865
Then don't bother asking.

384
00:26:47,465 --> 00:26:51,345
You were capable enough to take
the Qipai project from us.

385
00:26:52,465 --> 00:26:55,265
Surely you're capable enough
to handle it yourselves.

386
00:26:58,425 --> 00:27:00,265
And now you have the nerve
to ask us for the files?

387
00:27:00,345 --> 00:27:03,505
Didn't your mother teach you that thieves
get what's coming to them?

388
00:27:05,185 --> 00:27:06,385
Keep up the good work.

389
00:27:08,545 --> 00:27:10,585
This is an office,
not your neighborhood market.

390
00:27:10,665 --> 00:27:11,785
We're all colleagues.

391
00:27:11,865 --> 00:27:13,345
Watch your mouth.

392
00:27:14,385 --> 00:27:16,105
A vicious dog always gets
what's coming to it.

393
00:27:16,185 --> 00:27:17,985
Enjoy your little win while it lasts.

394
00:27:18,065 --> 00:27:19,665
Have some dignity, will you?

395
00:27:19,745 --> 00:27:21,105
Come looking for trouble again,

396
00:27:21,905 --> 00:27:23,185
and you'll regret it.

397
00:27:23,265 --> 00:27:24,385
Get lost.

398
00:27:30,825 --> 00:27:32,185
Send me the files.

399
00:27:46,305 --> 00:27:47,145
Is this for me?

400
00:27:47,665 --> 00:27:48,745
Thanks.

401
00:27:51,025 --> 00:27:52,145
Lumi,

402
00:27:53,145 --> 00:27:55,065
I didn't know switching teams
would cause all this.

403
00:27:55,145 --> 00:27:57,505
And I had no idea
that things were so tense

404
00:27:58,345 --> 00:27:59,305
between you and Alex's team.

405
00:27:59,385 --> 00:28:01,785
Had I known--

406
00:28:01,865 --> 00:28:05,065
You haven't been here long enough
to know all the bad blood between us.

407
00:28:05,145 --> 00:28:07,185
This company is full
of competing interests.

408
00:28:07,265 --> 00:28:09,025
Taking sides is unavoidable.

409
00:28:11,505 --> 00:28:13,825
You don't need to feel guilty.

410
00:28:13,905 --> 00:28:15,425
Just focus on your own work.

411
00:28:15,945 --> 00:28:18,865
They gave me an impossible task.

412
00:28:22,705 --> 00:28:25,345
They told you to ask Luke
for the source files?

413
00:28:26,865 --> 00:28:27,985
Damn it.

414
00:28:28,865 --> 00:28:30,225
They really know how to pick
an easy target.

415
00:28:32,625 --> 00:28:34,065
I can't help you with this.

416
00:28:34,145 --> 00:28:35,585
Luke always keeps
the source files himself.

417
00:28:35,665 --> 00:28:36,505
They never pass through me.

418
00:28:37,305 --> 00:28:38,465
My advice?

419
00:28:38,545 --> 00:28:41,385
Turn this task down,
or it could blow up in your face.

420
00:28:43,105 --> 00:28:44,585
I… I understand.

421
00:28:46,345 --> 00:28:50,665
Save this cake for the kids.

422
00:29:08,705 --> 00:29:10,945
DU ANNI: REPORT BACK BY TOMORROW

423
00:29:15,105 --> 00:29:16,585
LINGDONG SQUASH CENTER

424
00:29:16,665 --> 00:29:18,385
He broke the rules first,

425
00:29:18,465 --> 00:29:20,265
so there's nothing wrong
with you venting a little.

426
00:29:21,265 --> 00:29:24,465
Bottling it all up
isn't good for your health.

427
00:29:25,305 --> 00:29:28,225
And this will help
set things straight at Lime.

428
00:29:30,545 --> 00:29:32,145
Are you here to back Alex up, Mr. Lin?

429
00:29:33,625 --> 00:29:34,665
I'm not taking anyone's side.

430
00:29:34,745 --> 00:29:35,985
I'm only thinking of Lime.

431
00:29:36,505 --> 00:29:37,865
Don't worry.

432
00:29:37,945 --> 00:29:39,705
Wherever the Qipai project goes,

433
00:29:39,785 --> 00:29:40,985
it'll stay within Lime.

434
00:29:41,065 --> 00:29:41,985
We won't lose it.

435
00:29:43,905 --> 00:29:44,785
Good.

436
00:29:45,305 --> 00:29:48,825
And I never shortchange
employees who see the bigger picture.

437
00:29:49,345 --> 00:29:51,625
There's an awards ceremony next week.
Come with me.

438
00:29:51,705 --> 00:29:55,145
I'll give you projects from several
of Lime's longtime clients.

439
00:29:55,225 --> 00:29:56,705
They'll be every bit as good as Qipai.

440
00:29:57,545 --> 00:29:59,985
-OK.
-Want to grab a drink afterward?

441
00:30:06,025 --> 00:30:06,865
TAOBAO

442
00:30:06,945 --> 00:30:08,665
-Hello. Your food delivery.
-Thanks.

443
00:30:17,905 --> 00:30:19,065
What's wrong?

444
00:30:19,145 --> 00:30:20,945
Why are you taking it out on that radish?

445
00:30:22,105 --> 00:30:23,385
I don't think

446
00:30:24,585 --> 00:30:26,905
I can keep doing this job.

447
00:30:26,985 --> 00:30:30,905
My boss wants me to get the files
from Luan Nian

448
00:30:30,985 --> 00:30:34,505
to prove my worth to the new team.

449
00:30:37,665 --> 00:30:38,625
Let me ask you this.

450
00:30:39,145 --> 00:30:40,705
Do you still want to stay at Lime?

451
00:30:42,905 --> 00:30:44,025
Of course I do.

452
00:30:44,105 --> 00:30:45,505
Then there's your answer.

453
00:30:45,585 --> 00:30:48,345
Aren't you two back
to a normal working relationship now?

454
00:30:48,945 --> 00:30:52,625
Asking him for a file
is a perfectly normal work interaction.

455
00:30:53,385 --> 00:30:54,265
Tao,

456
00:30:54,985 --> 00:30:57,625
stop questioning yourself
and overthinking everything.

457
00:30:57,705 --> 00:31:02,185
What you should be figuring out now
is how to get the files

458
00:31:02,865 --> 00:31:04,025
and finish your job.

459
00:31:09,825 --> 00:31:10,825
You're right.

460
00:31:14,105 --> 00:31:15,265
Right.

461
00:31:24,265 --> 00:31:27,985
You need to remember whose team you're on.

462
00:31:28,065 --> 00:31:30,465
Fine. Go back and tell him

463
00:31:30,545 --> 00:31:31,945
I won't give them to you.

464
00:31:32,025 --> 00:31:33,105
What do you think he'll say?

465
00:31:33,985 --> 00:31:35,705
<i>Probably the same thing you did.</i>

466
00:31:35,785 --> 00:31:36,985
<i>He'll want me to quit.</i>

467
00:31:48,465 --> 00:31:49,465
Luke.

468
00:31:49,985 --> 00:31:53,385
I apologize for how I acted
this afternoon,

469
00:31:53,945 --> 00:31:55,865
but I really need the source files.

470
00:31:55,945 --> 00:31:57,345
I know this isn't right,

471
00:31:57,425 --> 00:31:59,065
-but could you…?
-Shang Zhitao.

472
00:32:01,425 --> 00:32:02,345
Enter the code for me.

473
00:32:15,265 --> 00:32:16,465
What is it?

474
00:32:17,185 --> 00:32:18,305
Seven-zero-eight-zero-zero.

475
00:32:22,425 --> 00:32:24,705
<i>Verified. Please open the door.</i>

476
00:33:08,425 --> 00:33:09,625
Shang Zhitao.

477
00:33:20,305 --> 00:33:21,665
What are you doing?

478
00:33:28,025 --> 00:33:28,865
Luke.

479
00:33:29,905 --> 00:33:30,865
Don't talk.

480
00:33:59,185 --> 00:34:01,185
<i>After alcohol hits,</i>

481
00:34:01,265 --> 00:34:04,705
<i>there's usually a half-hour</i>
<i>transition period.</i>

482
00:34:05,265 --> 00:34:06,785
<i>During that half hour,</i>

483
00:34:07,425 --> 00:34:11,945
<i>everything a person does</i>
<i>is a mix of reason and confusion.</i>

484
00:34:12,705 --> 00:34:16,105
<i>At times like this,</i>
<i>anyone of the opposite sex</i>

485
00:34:16,705 --> 00:34:18,304
<i>looks more attractive than usual.</i>

486
00:34:19,185 --> 00:34:20,344
<i>He's just drunk.</i>

487
00:34:46,865 --> 00:34:48,065
Shang Zhitao.

488
00:34:53,824 --> 00:34:54,784
You're awake.

489
00:34:57,785 --> 00:34:59,105
You stayed here all night?

490
00:35:00,145 --> 00:35:01,745
I was going to leave yesterday,

491
00:35:02,465 --> 00:35:03,985
but then you threw up.

492
00:35:04,065 --> 00:35:05,585
I was worried something
might happen to you.

493
00:35:05,665 --> 00:35:07,105
Plus,

494
00:35:07,185 --> 00:35:09,145
I'd been up dealing with you all night
and was exhausted,

495
00:35:09,225 --> 00:35:10,065
so I fell asleep.

496
00:35:10,665 --> 00:35:11,625
Did you change my clothes?

497
00:35:12,785 --> 00:35:14,985
Yes. You threw up all over yourself
last night,

498
00:35:15,065 --> 00:35:16,105
so I changed them for you.

499
00:35:16,705 --> 00:35:18,225
Then I washed both our clothes.

500
00:35:18,825 --> 00:35:19,865
Don't get the wrong idea.

501
00:35:21,705 --> 00:35:22,665
Fine.

502
00:35:23,225 --> 00:35:24,505
-I'm going to take a shower.
-Luke,

503
00:35:25,345 --> 00:35:26,185
the previous proposal…

504
00:36:16,625 --> 00:36:19,705
The client from Qipai
wants to use the previous proposal.

505
00:36:20,345 --> 00:36:23,945
Could you share the source files with us?

506
00:36:24,945 --> 00:36:27,105
But I really need the source files.

507
00:36:44,665 --> 00:36:45,505
Hello?

508
00:36:46,145 --> 00:36:47,345
Where are you?

509
00:36:47,425 --> 00:36:49,265
<i>I'm on my way to the bus stop.</i>

510
00:36:51,105 --> 00:36:52,305
Come back now.

511
00:36:54,865 --> 00:36:56,265
-Now?
-<i>Now.</i>

512
00:36:58,105 --> 00:36:59,145
I can't.

513
00:36:59,225 --> 00:37:01,145
<i>I need to go home and get ready,</i>

514
00:37:01,225 --> 00:37:02,825
-<i>then head to the office--</i>
-Come back now.

515
00:37:02,905 --> 00:37:04,345
Something's missing from my place.

516
00:37:24,225 --> 00:37:25,145
Sorry.

517
00:37:25,225 --> 00:37:27,665
It was chilly when I left,

518
00:37:27,745 --> 00:37:29,585
and my clothes were still wet,

519
00:37:29,665 --> 00:37:31,185
so I borrowed one of your coats.

520
00:37:31,265 --> 00:37:32,985
If you don't want to lend it to me,

521
00:37:33,065 --> 00:37:34,905
I'll take it off right now.

522
00:37:34,985 --> 00:37:36,265
That's not what's missing.

523
00:37:36,905 --> 00:37:39,425
Then, what is?

524
00:37:39,505 --> 00:37:41,065
My safe was broken into.

525
00:37:41,585 --> 00:37:42,705
The diamond is gone.

526
00:37:42,785 --> 00:37:45,785
I don't even know where your safe is.

527
00:37:48,905 --> 00:37:50,185
You must have security cameras.

528
00:37:50,265 --> 00:37:51,985
Why don't we check the footage?

529
00:37:54,905 --> 00:37:57,105
I'm kidding. Come in.

530
00:37:59,305 --> 00:38:02,105
-I need to shower before going to work.
-Why are you in such a rush?

531
00:38:02,625 --> 00:38:03,905
Have you finished your assignment?

532
00:38:07,905 --> 00:38:08,825
Did you bring the USB drive?

533
00:38:14,945 --> 00:38:16,545
<i>ENGLISH-CHINESE &amp;</i>
<i>CHINESE-ENGLISH ADVERTISING TERMINOLOGY</i>

534
00:38:18,625 --> 00:38:20,105
Still brushing up on your English?

535
00:38:20,185 --> 00:38:21,585
Worried Lime will fire you,

536
00:38:22,105 --> 00:38:23,225
and you won't find a better job?

537
00:38:25,225 --> 00:38:26,105
Here it is.

538
00:38:49,905 --> 00:38:51,705
The source files for the Qipai project?

539
00:38:52,385 --> 00:38:53,345
Sit down and wait.

540
00:38:53,865 --> 00:38:54,785
The files are huge.

541
00:38:55,425 --> 00:38:56,705
It'll take 40 minutes to copy them.

542
00:39:00,025 --> 00:39:01,185
Thank you, Luke.

543
00:39:01,265 --> 00:39:02,905
Thank you so, so much.

544
00:39:03,425 --> 00:39:04,265
I'll wait outside.

545
00:39:05,065 --> 00:39:08,185
Will waiting outside
make the transfer any faster?

546
00:39:09,065 --> 00:39:10,505
If you want them, don't chicken out.

547
00:39:18,745 --> 00:39:21,425
You can make slides, right?
Format a deck for me.

548
00:39:21,505 --> 00:39:23,985
I want the final version by 10 a.m.

549
00:39:24,785 --> 00:39:26,305
Sure. I can do that.

550
00:39:56,345 --> 00:39:59,065
The clothes from last night are dry now.

551
00:39:59,145 --> 00:40:00,225
Go shower in the guest room.

552
00:40:00,945 --> 00:40:01,825
Then eat breakfast before you leave.

553
00:40:03,065 --> 00:40:03,905
It's all right.

554
00:40:03,985 --> 00:40:05,345
It's not like you haven't
showered here before.

555
00:40:07,425 --> 00:40:08,865
Do you want to go to work smelling awful?

556
00:40:10,465 --> 00:40:12,425
OK, I… I'll go shower now.

557
00:40:22,945 --> 00:40:24,065
Can you drive?

558
00:40:25,705 --> 00:40:26,545
No.

559
00:40:26,625 --> 00:40:27,585
You can't?

560
00:40:28,505 --> 00:40:29,705
If you collect seven things you can't do,

561
00:40:29,785 --> 00:40:31,225
will Shenron grant you a promotion?

562
00:40:32,265 --> 00:40:35,825
Do you need to pass a driving test
to get promoted at Lime?

563
00:40:36,585 --> 00:40:38,865
Not for promotion,
but you need to drive for the job.

564
00:40:39,945 --> 00:40:40,905
Can't you drive today?

565
00:40:42,065 --> 00:40:43,585
The alcohol hasn't fully metabolized yet.

566
00:40:43,665 --> 00:40:44,505
It'd count as drunk driving.

567
00:40:46,665 --> 00:40:48,345
I'll get a cab. We'll go together.

568
00:40:51,025 --> 00:40:52,025
All right.

569
00:41:02,585 --> 00:41:04,105
YUETENG AUTO INTRODUCTION

570
00:41:04,185 --> 00:41:05,145
YUETENG 5.0 CHURN ANALYSIS

571
00:41:05,225 --> 00:41:06,825
YUETENG 5.0 TARGET USER PROFILE

572
00:41:11,145 --> 00:41:12,385
How is it?

573
00:41:18,185 --> 00:41:19,865
The gold should be glaring like this,

574
00:41:19,945 --> 00:41:22,305
like a car hood baking in the summer sun.

575
00:41:22,385 --> 00:41:24,025
Don't use cheap phrases
like "value for money" in the title.

576
00:41:24,105 --> 00:41:26,065
Focus on how it elevates
the owner's status.

577
00:41:26,145 --> 00:41:28,025
Isn't that a little over the top?

578
00:41:28,105 --> 00:41:30,425
Advertising is all about being
over the top.

579
00:41:30,505 --> 00:41:32,265
Learn from competing proposals.

580
00:41:33,025 --> 00:41:35,705
This was last year's winning campaign,
done in laser gold.

581
00:41:35,785 --> 00:41:36,585
CORE STRATEGY
BROAD REACH, FAST IGNITION

582
00:41:42,105 --> 00:41:43,385
Go learn to drive.

583
00:41:44,465 --> 00:41:46,465
A driver's license is a must at Lime.

584
00:41:46,545 --> 00:41:48,945
Auto brand campaigns
make up over half of Lime's revenue.

585
00:41:49,025 --> 00:41:50,665
Without knowing how to drive,

586
00:41:50,745 --> 00:41:52,345
you can't even gain proper
customer insight.

587
00:41:52,985 --> 00:41:55,065
Even if I could drive,
I still wouldn't have a car.

588
00:41:55,745 --> 00:41:57,465
If you never learn to drive,
you'll never have one.

589
00:42:06,105 --> 00:42:07,145
Luke,

590
00:42:08,665 --> 00:42:10,225
could you let me get out first
when we get there?

591
00:42:12,545 --> 00:42:14,345
Is it embarrassing to be seen with me?

592
00:42:15,545 --> 00:42:16,625
No, it's not.

593
00:42:17,625 --> 00:42:20,585
I just don't want
any unnecessary misunderstandings.

594
00:42:21,905 --> 00:42:23,865
You dared to come to my place
for the files,

595
00:42:23,945 --> 00:42:26,185
but you're afraid of gossip
over sharing a ride?

596
00:42:49,425 --> 00:42:50,665
Get out.

597
00:43:10,825 --> 00:43:12,425
Not bad.

598
00:43:17,705 --> 00:43:19,625
So you really are on good terms with Luke.

599
00:43:46,065 --> 00:43:46,905
Hello.

600
00:43:52,905 --> 00:43:53,985
-Thanks.
-Go ahead.

601
00:44:07,105 --> 00:44:09,185
-Luke, our…
-Shang Zhitao.

602
00:44:11,545 --> 00:44:12,705
Enter the code for me.

603
00:44:14,785 --> 00:44:15,905
Seven-zero-eight-zero-zero.

604
00:44:25,665 --> 00:44:27,985
-<i>Verification failed.</i>
-What was it?

605
00:44:36,145 --> 00:44:38,425
<i>Verified. Please open the door.</i>

